<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia Feb 1-25 palm oil exports 360,382t - SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia Feb 1-25 palm oil exports 360,382t - SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for February 1-25 at 360,382 tonnes against 401,932 in January 1-25.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 151,255 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 127,773 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 34,550 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products were 46,804 tonnes.  </p>
<p>Pakistan was the main buyer during the period, taking 85,300 tonnes, followed by Jordan 34,380 tonnes, Japan 30,440 tonnes and India 26,920.</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 48,914 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-7510)</p>
</text>
